        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ناگهان",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ناگهان (nâgahân) — \"suddenly, all of a sudden\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ناگهان (nâgahân) برق رفت و خانه تاریک شد. Nâgahân barq raft va khâne târik shod. Suddenly the power went off and the house went dark."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neutral and common in stories; in everyday speech Iranians also say yekhow. It usually opens the clause."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "nâgahân is inherited: EtymDB derives it from nâgah (also nâgâh), which continues Middle Persian anāgāh, \"unaware, unwitting\". A sudden thing comes on you unawares."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
