          "title": "You'll want to know: بلافاصله",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بلافاصله (belâfâsele) — \"immediately, right away\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پلیس بلافاصله به محل رسید. Polis belâfâsele be mahal resid. The police arrived at the scene immediately."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Literally \"without a gap\". Belâfâsele ba'd az means \"right after\": belâfâsele ba'd az shâm \"right after dinner\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "belâfâsele is an Arabic phrase taken over whole: bi- \"with\", lā \"no\" and fāṣila \"an interval, a gap\" (EtymDB lists Arabic fāṣila). Persian uses it as a single adverb."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
