          "title": "You'll want to know: همین که",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "همین که (hamin ke) — \"the moment that, as soon as\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "همین که (hamin ke) در را باز کردم، گربه فرار کرد. Hamin ke dar râ bâz kardam, gorbe farâr kard. The moment I opened the door, the cat ran away."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It opens a clause, with the past for a past event: hamin ke residam \"as soon as I arrived\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "hamin ke joins hamin \"this very\", built on ham \"same, also\" and in \"this\", with the linking word ke \"that\". All of its parts are inherited Persian words."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
