          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اتفاقی (ettefâqi) — \"by chance, accidentally\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "دیروز اتفاقی دوست مدرسه ام را در بازار دیدم. Diruz ettefâqi dust-e madrese-am râ dar bâzâr didam. Yesterday I ran into my school friend at the bazaar by chance."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also an adjective: yek didâr-e ettefâqi \"a chance meeting\". Built on ettefâq \"an event\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ettefâqi adds the Persian suffix -i to ettefâq \"an event\", which is borrowed from Arabic ittifāq (EtymDB). In Arabic the word is usually glossed \"agreement, coincidence\"."
            }
          ]
        },
